{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789744054,"nonce":"1YdfEgURg7SUxCNivFeQs6QNQvg=","title":"ash_core does not build as a git dependency: its build script embeds a cdylib built out of band","message":"crates/ash/build.rs embeds `libash_std.dylib` (`.so`, `.dll`) read from\n`\u003ccheckout\u003e/target/\u003cprofile\u003e/`, or `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`, and panics when\nnone is there (\"Build it first: cargo build -p ash_std\"). A dependent\nthat names ash by git rev gets the sources in cargo's git checkout,\nwhere no target directory exists and ash_std is built as an rlib only,\nso ash_core's build fails before the dependent compiles a line. caribou\npins `rev = 7932bb5` for ash_std, ash_native_call, ash_core and\nash_interp and has to keep a `[patch]` to a sibling checkout for that\nreason alone (its root Cargo.toml says so).\n\nTwo ways through: the build script builds the cdylib itself when none is\nfound (a nested `cargo build -p ash_std --lib` into a target directory\nof its own under OUT_DIR, once), or the embedded runtime becomes a\nfeature, on for ash's own binary and off for a host that stages nothing\nbeside a program. The staging path (`write_embedded_runtime`, used on\nmacOS when HDLLs sit beside the program) needs the bytes in either case.","files":null}]}